                                                                                
 Usage: python -m aeep [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...                              
                                                                                
 Profile and route agent actions across Python, CLI, HTTP, MCP, and host        
 agents.                                                                        
                                                                                
╭─ Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ --install-completion          Install completion for the current shell.      │
│ --show-completion             Show completion for the current shell, to copy │
│                               it or customize the installation.              │
│ --help                        Show this message and exit.                    │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭─ Commands ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ update                                                                       │
│ uninstall                                                                    │
│ setup                                                                        │
│ discover                                                                     │
│ init-assessment  Create a selected-plugin assessment and exact review        │
│                  bundle; execute nothing.                                    │
│ version          Print the package version.                                  │
│ init             Create a runnable manifest with equivalent Python and CLI   │
│                  routes.                                                     │
│ doctor           Validate the manifest and check local integration           │
│                  prerequisites.                                              │
│ list             List capabilities and configured execution routes.          │
│ search           Search capabilities without loading every executor into the │
│                  response.                                                   │
│ policies         List built-in and manifest-defined policies.                │
│ metrics          Summarize execution savings and subscription capacity       │
│                  conserved.                                                  │
│ quote            Request bounded static/provider quotes without accepting    │
│                  payment.                                                    │
│ run-prepared     Execute one immutable prepared route after rechecking its   │
│                  original action.                                            │
│ accept-quote     Explicitly accept one stored quote; this is not exposed as  │
│                  a model tool.                                               │
│ sign-receipt     Sign a persisted receipt with the operator-configured local │
│                  identity.                                                   │
│ counterfactual   Show feasible routes that could have avoided observed cost  │
│                  or scarcity.                                                │
│ reputation       Aggregate measured or verified outcomes; provider claims    │
│                  are excluded.                                               │
│ reserve-payment  Reserve funds under the operator budget and financial       │
│                  approval ceiling.                                           │
│ capture-payment  Capture a previously approved reservation after delivery.   │
│ refund-payment   Refund a captured payment through the configured adapter.   │
│ route            Rank execution alternatives without invoking one.           │
│ host-bridge      Serve the bounded local JSONL protocol used by native host  │
│                  adapters.                                                   │
│ run              Route, invoke, validate, persist a receipt, and safely fall │
│                  back.                                                       │
│ benchmark        Execute alternatives sequentially to calibrate actual       │
│                  cost/time/compute.                                          │
│ history          Inspect persisted decisions or observed execution receipts. │
│ show             Fetch one persisted decision or receipt.                    │
│ record           Record the actual outcome of a delegated                    │
│                  browser/model/computer-use route.                           │
│ tool-call        Invoke an AEEP tool over deterministic JSON without running │
│                  an MCP server.                                              │
│ publish          Generate a local provider descriptor; network publication   │
│                  is registry-specific.                                       │
│ serve            Expose AEEP as an MCP server for ChatGPT/Codex, Claude, or  │
│                  OpenClaw.                                                   │
│ assess           Propose, review and run bounded plugin assessments.         │
│ task             Enable, inspect, pause and remove project-local task        │
│                  activations.                                                │
│ stack            Propose compatible configurations, inspect setup, and       │
│                  execute reviewed stacks.                                    │
│ agents           Connect agents and inspect or adopt native tool controls.   │
│ access           Restrict tool exposure and calls without enlarging          │
│                  execution authority.                                        │
│ catalogs         Manage searchable metadata sources; never install their     │
│                  plugins automatically.                                      │
│ tools            Export AEEP as native tools for agent providers.            │
│ import           Import existing CLI, MCP, or OpenAPI capabilities.          │
│ subscriptions    Manage user-owned model and tool subscriptions.             │
│ quota            Set or observe subscription quota pressure.                 │
│ skill            Install the packaged AEEP skill into an agent host.         │
│ ingest           Ingest traces from existing agent runtimes.                 │
│ candidate        Qualify and activate inert imported routes.                 │
│ provider         Validate, digest, verify, and sign provider packages.       │
│ evidence         Inspect accepted portable provider evidence.                │
│ registry         Search bounded provider-package registry metadata.          │
│ workflow         Run caller-authored bounded workflows.                      │
│ campaign         Run isolated repeated benchmark campaigns.                  │
│ offer            Inspect and import signed capability offers.                │
│ economic         Prepare routes and inspect economic evidence.               │
│ settlement       Inspect and reconcile settlement evidence.                  │
│ market           Run the local reference economic market.                    │
│ x402             Run optional offline x402 capacity conformance.             │
│ hosts            Inspect locally configured managed hosts.                   │
│ capacity         Inspect provider-neutral capacity state.                    │
│ verify           Run digest-bound executable completion checks.              │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

